WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.860
- It's nice to see you again.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.510
- Nice to see you.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.250
- The last time I saw you,
you didn't have a kid.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.083
You have a two year old now.

00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:07.800
- And you didn't have an Emmy.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:08.854
- Well, boom.

00:00:08.854 --> 00:00:09.687
(audience clapping)

00:00:09.687 --> 00:00:10.520
- Well and a baby.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.353
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:11.353 --> 00:00:12.186
I mean, that's not doing too bad.

00:00:12.186 --> 00:00:13.019
- We're killing it.

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:14.280
That's how is it, two, right?

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.113
Two years old.

00:00:15.113 --> 00:00:15.946
- She's two years old.

00:00:15.946 --> 00:00:18.690
I was pretty much pregnant
during the whole pandemic.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:19.523
- Wow.

00:00:19.523 --> 00:00:21.030
- Great way to keep it a secret

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.010
'cause all your meetings
are from here up, you know.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.150
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, that's awesome.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.050
- Yeah.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.613
And I had a daughter.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.299
Yeah, in August of 2020.

00:00:29.299 --> 00:00:30.132
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:00:30.132 --> 00:00:30.965
- Yeah.

00:00:30.965 --> 00:00:31.798
- That's so cool.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.631
- Yeah, it was the best.

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:33.464
- [Kelly] I'm very happy for you.

00:00:33.464 --> 00:00:34.500
I have kiddos and there's
six and eight now,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.910
but that's magical.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.360
Every step is challenging but
every step is magical as well.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.200
But being,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.000
being a first time parent
can be hard though.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.370
So who's your go-to for advice?

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.685
- I mean, I have a
couple little mom groups.

00:00:46.685 --> 00:00:47.518
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:47.518 --> 00:00:50.010
- Mom friends and then
my own mom, of course.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.320
- [Kelly] Yeah. I hope so as well.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.340
You went through a challenging time

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.420
with your mama, right?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.332
- Yeah.

00:00:55.332 --> 00:00:56.520
- I mean, I feel like I could have asked

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.353
any of us that question.

00:00:57.353 --> 00:00:58.186
(audience laughing)

00:00:58.186 --> 00:00:59.019
- I know, right?

00:00:59.019 --> 00:01:00.360
- I feel like we all even are
mothers with their mothers.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.193
Yeah.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.610
- The relationship is such a journey

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.020
and that's what's beautiful about it.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.600
But you know, it's one
of the things I write

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.880
about in my book that
I was really ashamed of

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.270
and embarrassed for a long time is that,

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.550
I was, like estranged
from my mother for like

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.540
five, six years.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.440
Didn't speak to her.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.568
- Wow.

00:01:17.568 --> 00:01:18.401
- Not even in email.

00:01:18.401 --> 00:01:19.890
And that's on me.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.750
And the beautiful thing

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.730
about becoming pregnant was,

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.590
it sort of brought us together again

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.150
and we've reconciled since then.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:27.983
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:30.630
- And, you know, continue
building a wonderful relationship.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.090
- Yeah. It gives you a fresh
perspective on parenting too.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.302
- Oh, 100%.

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:35.135
- Yeah.

00:01:35.135 --> 00:01:35.968
- 'Cause my mom had four.

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:36.892
- Yeah.

00:01:36.892 --> 00:01:37.725
- And I only have one

00:01:37.725 --> 00:01:38.640
and I'm like, how do you?

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.840
- Yeah, my mom had three

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.227
and I two and I'm just like, whoa.

00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:42.753
You're outnumbered.

